# Keep Cline out of files that will blow a 32k context window.
#
# The box loads qwen3-30b-a3b-2507 with a 32,768-token window. A single
# bundled file in node_modules (rollup.js and friends) is larger than that on
# its own, so one stray read ends the task with "Context size has been
# exceeded" and no way to recover except starting over. A `find . -name "*.js"`
# walks straight into them, which is exactly what happened.
#
# This is about context budget, not secrecy — everything here is either
# generated, vendored, or binary, and none of it is worth spending the window
# on when the answer is always in src/.

node_modules/
dist/
build/
.next/
coverage/

# Lockfiles: enormous, generated, and never the thing you are asking about.
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Build and editor noise
.git/
.DS_Store
*.log
.vite/
.cache/

# Binaries and documents — unreadable as text and expensive to try
*.pdf
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
*.ico
*.woff
*.woff2
*.ttf
*.zip
*.mp4
*.mp3
